<section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow" data-i18n="ld.eyebrow">Live demo · A real, read-only sandbox of the app <span class="pill pill-built" data-i18n="ld.pill">No login</span></p>
      <h1 data-i18n="ld.h1">Try openWCS right here, <span class="lime">no sign-up, nothing saved.</span></h1>
      <p class="lead" data-i18n="ld.lead">
        This is the real openWCS app running entirely in your browser as a read-only sandbox. Open every
        menu and browse the actual screens with sample data, but nothing can be changed and nothing is
        saved anywhere. Reloading the page resets the demo to its starting point. The headline interaction
        is the goods-to-person pick station: five totes arrive and you can pick them, full pick or short
        pick, including the normal exceptions.
      </p>
      <div class="grid grid-3">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-head"><div class="tag" data-i18n="ld.point1Tag">Read-only</div></div>
          <h3 data-i18n="ld.point1H">Browse everything, change nothing</h3>
          <p data-i18n="ld.point1P">Every menu opens and every screen renders with sample data, but all create, edit and delete controls are disabled. You cannot break anything.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-head"><div class="tag" data-i18n="ld.point2Tag">Nothing saved</div></div>
          <h3 data-i18n="ld.point2H">It all lives in your browser</h3>
          <p data-i18n="ld.point2P">There is no backend and no database behind this demo. All state is in memory, so a page reload restores the original sample data and re-arms the five totes.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-head"><div class="tag" data-i18n="ld.point3Tag">Pick five totes</div></div>
          <h3 data-i18n="ld.point3H">The goods-to-person station</h3>
          <p data-i18n="ld.point3P">Five totes arrive at the pick station. Present and confirm each one as a full pick or a short pick, trigger the usual exceptions, and reset to run it again.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

